      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **[[write-journal]]** page describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\nBefore the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 whether it previously existed and what its content was, or that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. If an agent run later fails (due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or all attempted writes being denied), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: it restores previous content for files that existed and deletes files that were newly created.\n\nThis design gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held only in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run. The page notes that the Query agent never uses this rollback path since it has no write tool at all, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
